# Text and Paragraph: the text in the value or in a Content block, where a single line break is a space.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Text and Paragraph · Value and Content
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: Text and Paragraph
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Value and Content
		Paragraph: A short text goes in the value. A long one goes in a `Content >>` block, where each line break counts as a space, so the source lines can be broken anywhere. A blank line inside `Content` is an error: several paragraphs are several `Paragraph`.
			Style: intro
		Text: Paragraph: Kind regards.
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Kind regards.
			Style: sample
		Text: Paragraph: with Content >> in four source lines
			Style: label
		Paragraph:
			Style: sample
			Content >>
				The Saturday market returns to the main square
				with more stalls than ever: vegetables from the gardens,
				cheese from the hills and bread from the wood oven.
				The four source lines make one paragraph.
		Text: Text: with Content >> in two source lines
			Style: label
		Text:
			Style: sample
			Content >>
				A Text also accepts Content: these two source lines
				are joined by a space.
